The assessment called #885 stale-done. It isn't. The gate half landed (19 classify_shrink hits), but extract_trajectory.py:1752 is still `elif lines > recorded:` — negative drift remains invisible to the loop's only reader, which is the exact thing #885's own remedy warned about. I nearly closed an issue by checking the half that was easy to grep for, which is the same shape as the defect the issue describes. It stays open with that correction; #834 and #835 close as genuinely done.
